.TH ZIMANYAR-LSP 1 "November 2026" "Zimanyar" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zimanyar\-lsp \- the Zimanyar language server, for checking Kurdish in any editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zimanyar\-lsp
.RB [ \-\-stdio ]
.br
.B zimanyar lsp
.RB [ \-\-stdio ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zimanyar\-lsp
speaks the Language Server Protocol over standard input and output. An editor starts it and receives
the mistakes in Sorani and Kurmanji text as diagnostics, a quick fix for each suggestion, a fix of
every safe spelling mistake at once (the code action kind
.BR source.fixAll.zimanyar ),
a hover that explains a mistake and links its lesson, and completion of Kurdish words.
.PP
Markdown documents are checked in their prose only: code, link targets and markup make no
diagnostics. Hints are sent with the severity Information, since many editors hide hints.
.PP
It runs entirely on your own computer: it never opens a network connection. It ends when the
editor closes its input.
.SH SETTINGS
Settings come in
.B initializationOptions
and in the
.B zimanyar
section of
.BR workspace/didChangeConfiguration .
A setting with the wrong shape is ignored.
.TP
.BR lang " (ckb, kmr or auto)"
The variety to check. auto, the default, chooses for each paragraph by its script and words.
.TP
.BR ui " (en, ckb or kmr)"
The language of messages. The default is chosen as for
.BR zimanyar (1).
.TP
.BR rules ", " disable " (lists of rule ids or prefixes)"
Run only these rules, and leave these out.
.TP
.BR tolerant " (true or false)"
Accept what is common in writing but outside the written standard.
.TP
.BR words " (list of words)"
Words to accept as spelled right: names, terms, a personal dictionary.
.SH EXAMPLES
Neovim 0.11:
.PP
.nf
vim.lsp.config("zimanyar", {
  cmd = { "zimanyar\-lsp" },
  filetypes = { "markdown", "text" },
  init_options = { ui = "kmr" },
})
vim.lsp.enable("zimanyar")
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zimanyar (1),
https://0xdolan.github.io/Zimanyar/
